course: dictionary
lesson: 12316
title: Matching things: corresponding
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Corresponding means matching, or connected with something else. When two things correspond, each one has a partner that goes with it. «Write each word next to its corresponding picture.» The word tells you that each picture has a matching word, so you draw a line between the pair.
explain: The word can also mean happening at the same time, or in the same way, as something else. «The corresponding week last term» means the matching week, at the same point in last term. Look at the words around it to see what is being matched: a picture, a week, a shape or a number.
explain: In maths, corresponding parts sit in the same position in two shapes or on two lines. When a line crosses two parallel lines, the corresponding angles are equal. Corresponding sides of similar shapes are in the same position, too. Always ask: matching what?
fact: Corresponding means matching or connected with something else.
fact: «Corresponding» can mean happening at the same time or in the same way, as in «a corresponding increase».
fact: In maths, corresponding angles are equal when a line crosses two parallel lines.
fact: In a science graph, each time has a corresponding temperature: the two numbers go together in pairs.
fact: As a verb, «corresponding» means writing letters or emails to someone, as in «We have been corresponding by email».
exercise: «Write each word next to its corresponding picture.» What does corresponding mean here? | Loud and noisy | Very large | Hidden under the table | *Matching or connected
exercise: In maths, corresponding angles are in the same position when a line crosses two parallel lines. What are they? | Longer than the lines | *Equal | Hidden from view | Always right angles
exercise: «A price rise and a corresponding fall in sales.» What does corresponding mean in this sentence? | A cheap bag of sweets | *A matching change that happens at the same time | A sound made by a drum | Something that is broken
test: «We have been corresponding by email.» What does corresponding mean here? | Sleeping in the car | Drawing pictures of fish | *Writing messages back and forth | Running a race
test: «The corresponding week last term.» What does this mean? | Any week at all | *The matching week, at the same point in a different term | The week before Christmas | A week with no lessons
exam: Which sentence uses corresponding to mean matching? | The sun was bright and hot | We walked home after school | The dog barked loudly at the postman | *Each sock has a corresponding pair
